    {
        "content": "<p>The linear construction algorithm for <code>DecidableEq</code> seems to handle such types fine:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">decEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linear_construction_threshold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bool_value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int_value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--works</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 627770325,
        "sender_full_name": "Arthur Adjedj",
        "timestamp": 1790685914
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wow that is amazing, thank you</p>\n<p>I see it also works for <code>Ord</code> via</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ord</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linear_construction_threshold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there some docs I point to for this?</p>",
        "id": 627786845,
        "sender_full_name": "awalterschulze",
        "timestamp": 1790688832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That feels more like an unintentional feature; <code>linear_construction_threshold</code> should technically not produce different results. I'm working on new deriving handlers though that will not have this problem</p>",
        "id": 627800905,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790691627
